WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
Welcome to our training on enrolling a brand in Amazon Brand Registry.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.000
At Amazon, brands can enjoy additional selling benefits,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.400
added protections, and greater control over their product detail pages

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.000
by enrolling in Brand Registry.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
To enroll a brand, you need to meet two basic requirements.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.400
You need a brand name or a logo that includes your brand name

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.400
permanently affixed to your products or packaging.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.600
You also need to be the owner of a registered trademark for that brand name or logo

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:38.600
or the owner of a Pending Trademark Application or Pending Trademark Registration.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.400
Note that registered agents aren't able to submit enrollment applications

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.800
on behalf of trademark owners.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.000
If you're using a registered trademark to enroll in Brand Registry,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.400
it has to be active and issued by the Designated Government Office

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.400
of a country where Amazon has a corresponding store.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.400
As a reminder, here's the full list.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.400
In the US, for example, trademarks for brand names and logos

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.400
are issued by the United States Patent and Trademark Office or USPTO.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.400
For more information about the trademarking process,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:18.400
see our Seller University video "Register a Trademark for your Brand".

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.400
If you're using a Pending Trademark Application to Enroll in Brand Registry,

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.400
it also needs to be secured from the Designated Government Office

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.400
of a country where Amazon has a corresponding store.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:37.400
You can get assistance securing a Pending Application through Amazon's IP Accelerator Program,

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.400
which is a network of Amazon trusted law firms.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.400
To learn more about the program,

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:49.400
watch our Seller University video "Register a Trademark through IP Accelerator"

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.400
or get started by visiting brandservices.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:52.900
amazon.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:53.400
com,

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:57.400
hovering over tools and clicking IP Accelerator.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:02.400
If you're using a Pending Trademark Registration to Enroll in Brand Registry,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.400
you need to secure it from one of the Designated Government Offices

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.400
that Amazon accepts Pending Registrations from.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.400
To check whether your Pending Registration can be used for Brand Registry Enrollment,

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:21.400
search Seller Central for Enrollment Guidelines for Accepted Trademark Offices.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.400
Click the link for the relevant Trademark Office,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:29.400
then look for information about Pending Registrations and Trademark Status.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:35.400
Note that if you're using a Pending Application or Registration to Enroll in Brand Registry,

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.400
you'll likely need to wait at least 48 hours after submitting your application

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:46.400
to the Trademark Office before you can begin the Enrollment Process with Amazon.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.400
If your brand meets the requirements for Enrollment,

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.400
you're ready to start the process.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:56.400
Begin by creating a Brand Registry account if you don't have one already.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.900
Visit brandregistry.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:58.650
amazon.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.400
com

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:06.400
and create your account using the same credentials you use to sign into Seller Central.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.400
This helps ensure you have full access for your brand when you sign in to either portal.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.400
If you have an individual selling account with Amazon,

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:20.400
we also recommend upgrading to a professional account when you Enroll in Brand Registry.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:27.011
A professional account can help you take advantage of the full range of benefits available to registered

00:03:27.011 --> 00:03:27.400
brands.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.400
If you have a Seller Central and a Vendor Central account,

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:38.929
make sure the credentials for both selling accounts are the same before creating your Brand Registry

00:03:38.929 --> 00:03:39.400
account.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.400
This helps sync access for all three accounts.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:50.400
After creating your Brand Registry account, sign in and click Enroll a Brand on your home page.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.400
Then on the next page, click the Enroll your Brand button.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.400
You'll be brought to the first section of the Enrollment form.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.400
Under Brand Information, you'll enter your Brand Name, select a Trademark Office,

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:08.400
and enter the Registration or Serial Number associated with your Trademark.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:14.400
In some cases, you may also be prompted to provide additional information or documents.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:21.400
When entering your Brand Name, make sure that it's an exact match for the Name or Mark Text

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:27.400
that's on your Trademark Certificate, Pending Application or Pending Registration.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:32.400
The name you enter on the Enrollment form should have the same letters and special characters,

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.400
as well as capitalization and spacing.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:41.400
A Brand Name can rarely be changed after it's been submitted to Brand Registry,

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.400
so be sure to check your entry against your Official Trademark.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:50.400
When selecting a Trademark Office, you'll only be able to make a single selection.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.400
If you want to add Trademarks for the offices of other countries,

00:04:54.400 --> 00:05:00.400
you'll be able to do so after your enrollment in Brand Registry has been approved.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:06.400
We recommend submitting Trademarks for each country-based Amazon Store you want to sell in.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:11.400
That's because, while Brand Registry only requires a single country's Trademark,

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:17.400
in order to enroll and sell the Brand in every Amazon Store worldwide,

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:24.400
the IP rights and legal protections of a government-verified trademark remain country-specific.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:28.400
When entering your Trademark Registration or Serial Number,

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:32.400
make sure it's an exact match for the number on your Trademark Certificate

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:37.400
or the number on your Pending Trademark Application or Registration.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.400
Then click the Verify button.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:45.622
After your Trademark Number is verified, you'll be prompted to upload a high-resolution image of

00:05:45.622 --> 00:05:46.400
your logo

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.400
if you're using a design mark.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.400
Make sure this image is an exact match for the design mark on your Trademark.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:58.400
And don't upload your full Trademark Certificate if you have one.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:02.400
Next, under Product Information, upload at least one image

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:08.400
that clearly shows your brand name or logo permanently affixed to your products or packaging.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:14.400
Use images that show products you sell or intend to sell in the Amazon Store.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.400
But don't use computer-generated images.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:24.011
After uploading your images, click the Next button to go to the second section of the Enrollment

00:06:24.011 --> 00:06:24.400
form,

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.400
where you'll provide information about your selling account.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:33.400
Start by confirming whether you're a seller, a vendor, or both.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:37.400
Check the box next to Seller if you have a Seller Central account

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:41.400
and use the Amazon Store to sell directly to end customers,

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:47.400
either by fulfilling orders yourself or through fulfillment by Amazon or FBA.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:52.400
Check the box next to Vendor if you also have a Vendor Central account

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:56.400
and sell products to Amazon as a third party.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.400
You'll see an option for neither, too.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:04.400
This is for brands that don't want to sell directly in the Amazon Store.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:10.400
They enroll in brand registry to confirm their intellectual property rights with Amazon.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:16.400
Then extend listing privileges and the eligibility to activate selling benefits to others.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:21.400
Don't select neither if you intend to sell in the Amazon Store

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.400
and haven't yet set up a selling account.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:31.400
Instead, create a selling account, then come back to brand registry to restart the enrollment process.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:35.400
Next, select the categories that your brand's products fall into.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:40.400
If your brand's products are already listed in the Amazon Store,

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.400
select each category that's been used to list them.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:49.400
You should also select any new categories that you intend to use for future product listings.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.400
If your brand has existing Amazon listings,

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:58.400
you should also provide the ASINs for your top selling products in each category.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:04.400
Select the relevant store, enter the ASIN, then click the Add button.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:10.400
If your brand has an official website or you have a storefront on another e-commerce site,

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.400
you should also provide relevant URLs.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:21.341
Providing top selling ASINs and relevant URLs helps brand registry identify your brand and process

00:08:21.341 --> 00:08:22.400
your enrollment.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:27.400
Click the Next button to go to the last section of the enrollment form

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:31.400
where you'll provide manufacturing and distribution information.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:36.400
You'll answer three questions that help us understand and protect your brand.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:42.400
In some cases, you may also be prompted to provide additional information or documents.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:48.400
If you sell your products to distributors, those are agents that supply goods to other businesses,

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.400
click Yes.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:54.400
You'll also need to select the countries where your brand's products are distributed.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:59.400
If you only sell directly to retailers or end customers, click No.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:05.518
Finally, confirm whether you license your trademarks to others who manufacture products associated

00:09:05.518 --> 00:09:07.400
with your intellectual property.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.400
Click Yes or No.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:15.400
Then click the Submit button to complete your enrollment application and send it to brand registry.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:22.543
After your application is submitted, brand registry will email a verification code to the trademark

00:09:22.543 --> 00:09:25.400
correspondent listed on your trademark record.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:32.032
You'll need to send that verification code back within 10 days using a case in your brand registry

00:09:32.032 --> 00:09:32.400
account.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:37.400
Be sure to retrieve your verification code promptly from your trademark correspondent

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:43.400
and make sure you don't reply to the email from brand registry to provide verification.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:49.400
You can only confirm receipt of your verification code using a brand registry case.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:55.400
When you have your verification code, sign in to brand registry and click Case Log.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:10:01.700
Then click the View or Respond button for the relevant case and reply to the message from brand

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:02.400
registry support,

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:07.400
providing the verification code and case ID for your application.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:12.400
After you submit your verification code, your application will be reviewed.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:20.050
You can check the status of your application anytime in brand registry by hovering over Manage and

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.400
clicking Brand Applications.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:27.295
When your enrollment reads Approved, you then have the option to add trademarks from the offices

00:10:27.295 --> 00:10:28.400
of other countries.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:35.400
In the brand registry portal, hover over Manage and click Manage Intellectual Property.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.400
Then click the Connect Trademark button.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:45.979
On the form, confirm your brand name, select a trademark office, and verify your trademark registration

00:10:45.979 --> 00:10:47.400
or serial number.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:50.400
Then click the Connect Trademark button.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:56.025
You can check the status of your additional trademark back on the Manage Intellectual Properties

00:10:56.025 --> 00:10:56.400
page.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:01.400
When Approved, it will move from the Request section to the Connected section.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:06.400
This concludes our training on Enrolling a Brand in Brand Registry.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:09.960
Thank you, and happy selling in the Amazon Store.
